From c7b061300877ece17460ad27a67f641151aa1575 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Sotraidis <56282582+chrissotraidis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:05:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gx: a module display list's textures resolve at the module's
 address

A display list kept in a linked module's data (Wind Waker's d_a_bwdg, Molgera's sand floor) names the module's own texture with SETIMAGE3, whose 24 bits drop the address's top bits: 0xC06A0DA0 >> 5 leaves 0x006A0DA0, unrelated MEM1, and the floor drew with whatever was there. HLE GXCallDisplayList now passes the list's guest address down (call_display_list_guest, falling back to call_display_list), and while the frontend parses a list at an address with 0x40000000 set, the texture slots it sets resolve at 0xC0000000 | that address. A host without module aliases reads that as MEM1's uncached mirror, the same memory as before.
